; NAME carries the ring as the CP865 byte 0x8F (OEM: matches the module
; table + the VINDèSEN.EXE filename); DESCRIPTION carries it as the
; CP1252 byte 0xE5, since that string is ANSI display text.  Both are
; intentional -- do not "normalise" them to one encoding.
NAME         VINDèSEN

DESCRIPTION  'VindÂsen - order management for canned wine'

EXETYPE      WINDOWS       ; required for all Windows applications

REALMODE                   ; Windows 1.x runs in real mode

CODE  PRELOAD MOVEABLE DISCARDABLE
; An application's automatic-data segment must be MULTIPLE (MULTIPLEDATA) so
; Windows builds a per-instance DGROUP at launch; SINGLE marks a shared
; library data segment and is wrong for a program.  FIXED is kept (preferred
; for the near-pointer-heavy C code).  NB: the earlier "not enough memory"
; load failure was NOT the data-segment attribute -- it was the NE
; errors-in-image bit (NEIERR) set by unresolved C-runtime file externals;
; see docs/win101-loader.md.  Using the KERNEL file API removed that.
DATA  PRELOAD FIXED MULTIPLE

HEAPSIZE     1024
STACKSIZE    8192          ; headroom for the order-detail dialog + file rewrite

; All functions called back by Windows must be exported.
EXPORTS
    MainWndProc   @1        ; main window procedure
    About         @2        ; "About" dialog procedure
    OrderDlgProc  @3        ; order-detail (accept/reject) dialog procedure
